The Skeleton component doesn't include "skeleton" in its className (it uses `animate-pulse ...`). This selector will return 0 elements and fail the test. Consider asserting on `.animate-pulse` elements (or another stable selector) instead.
```suggestion
    // Check for skeleton elements via their animate-pulse loading class
    const skeletons = container.querySelectorAll('.animate-pulse');
```

These stories render `type: 'list-view'`, but Storybook's `.storybook/preview.ts` doesn't import/register `@object-ui/plugin-list`, so the renderer will show "Unknown: list-view". Add a side-effect import for the plugin (either in Storybook preview or in this story file) so the component is registered before rendering.
```suggestion
import type { BaseSchema } from '@object-ui/types';
import '@object-ui/plugin-list';
```

The component doesn't render any class containing "warning" for the 80% capacity state (it uses `text-yellow-500` and an `AlertTriangle` icon). This selector will never match and the test will fail; assert on the actual rendered output instead (e.g., the `4 / 5` count and yellow styling / icon).
```suggestion
    const { container } = render(<KanbanEnhanced columns={columnsNearLimit} />);

    // Should show warning indicator (80% of 5 = 4)
    // Assert on the actual rendered output: capacity text and yellow warning styling
    expect(screen.getByText('4 / 5')).toBeInTheDocument();
    expect(container.querySelector('[class*="text-yellow-500"]')).toBeTruthy();
```

